      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and a single dose is typically capped at 1,000 properly 850 mg. At this dose, the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity is high, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 1,700 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, split in some other way.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
